  "answer": "This feature has been requested before. The main tracking ticket is PowerToys#21313, a utility that disables the keyboard, mouse and touchscreen while you clean them. PowerToys#33581 and PowerToys#42868 were closed as duplicates of it. PowerToys#44783 was closed as a duplicate of the broader request in #31856. The PowerToys team said on #21313 that there are currently no plans to build this into PowerToys, so you should not expect it soon. Adding a thumbs-up to #21313 is the best way to show interest. In the meantime, you can use one of these workarounds from the tickets: (1) on a laptop, disable the internal keyboard in Device Manager (Win+X > Device Manager > Keyboards > Disable) and re-enable it afterwards; (2) use a small third-party keyboard-cleaning/lock tool such as KeyboardToggle (the tool posted in #42868) or an AutoHotkey script; (3) unplug a USB keyboard or turn off Bluetooth."
 },
